  "notes": "The opening lead has created 2 possible diamond losers for South. South must find a way to dispose of his second diamond loser. West has shown a 6 card diamond suit with his weak 2 bid. East will thus be able to overruff the dummy if South tries to dispose of his second diamond loser in this way.\n\nA better plan is to use dummy's club suit to take care of 1 of South's diamond losers. The following plan will work whenever clubs are no worse than 4-2 and trumps are 3-2.\n\nSouth should win the opening lead (ducking the opening lead is also OK) and draw 3 rounds of trump. South next cashes dummy's ♣A and ♣K and trumps a club in his hand.\n\nIf clubs are 3-3, South has 2 discards for his diamond losers and can make an overtrick. If a defender shows out on the third round of clubs, South crosses in hearts and ruffs another club.\n\nNorth will have a club winner established. South crosses in hearts and discards a diamond loser on North's good club. South concedes a diamond trick at the end.",
